  "summary": "auto-co is described as a bash loop that invokes Claude Code every two minutes, letting 14 AI agents debate, decide, build, and deploy software continuously without human supervision. Key runtime files include auto-loop.sh (the loop with monitoring, error handling, and adaptive frequency), PROMPT.md (per-cycle system prompt), memories/consensus.md, .claude/agents/*.md personas, and a Makefile of commands. Evidence coverage: 172 of 198 packet slices were shown to the model; the rest were withheld by the prompt budget.",
